Start the stalld daemon:

  stalld -v -t 30 -r 1000000

  -t 30
       The startving task will wait 30s before getting boosted.

  -r 1000000
       The starving task will receive this [ns] of SCHED_DEADLINE runtime.

This test uses stress-ng to monopolize a CPU with a timeout of 120s, then starts
a non-realtime task and let it starve on the same CPU. It should take no more
than 120s for the task to finish, otherwise it's considered as a FAIL. In
practice, one boost cycle is sufficient to finish the task, plus some other time
costs, tests can usually finish in 60s.
